    title: "Eisenkot invites Netanyahu's party for Israeli coalition talks",
    summary: "Eisenkot invites Netanyahu's party for Israeli coalition talks Gadi Eisenkot, who is tasked with forming the next Israeli government, has invited the right-wing Likud party of caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu for coalition talks, his party said on Saturday. Eisenkot's centrist Yashar party said the talks, scheduled to begin on Sunday, reflected a \"genuine commitment to forming the broadest possible government\". Former military chief Eisenkot has until next month to form a government to replace Netanyahu, after the October election failed to deliver a clear majority for either bloc. Saturday's announcement comes as Eisenkot's wide-ranging camp faces divisions on whether to forge alliances with the ultra-Orthodox parties, or the Arab-led lists, or whether to form a national unity government with Netanyahu's bloc. \"In an effort to pursue every option for forming a new government, Yashar Chair Gadi Eisenkot has instructed the party's negotiating team to invite its Likud counterparts to a marathon series of talks beginning with the meeting already scheduled for tomorrow,\" the party said in a statement. Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot speaks during a press conference at the President's office in Jerusalem on 8 November 2026 (AFP)",
