    id: "51022172af4e4d194876",
    cat: "geopolitica",
    categories: ["geopolitica"],
    title: "Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace",
    summary: "Finland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list.",
    preview: "Finland says Russian helicopter violated its airspace November 21, 2026 Finland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list. A Russian helicopter is suspected of violating Finnish airspace, the Nordic country's Ministry of Defense said Saturday. The incident happened a few hours after a drone attack left a Russian cargo ship ablaze in the Gulf of Finland, the easternmost part of the Baltic Sea. What do we know?",
    body: "Finland says Russian helicopter violated its airspace\n\nNovember 21, 2026\n\nFinland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list.\n\nA Russian helicopter is suspected of violating Finnish airspace, the Nordic country's Ministry of Defense said Saturday.\n\nThe incident happened a few hours after a drone attack left a Russian cargo ship ablaze in the Gulf of Finland, the easternmost part of the Baltic Sea.\n\nWhat do we know?\n\nAccording to Finland's Defense Ministry, the incursion happened at 12:34 p.m. local time (10:34 UTC/GMT) off the town of Loviisa, on the southern coast.\n\n\"This alleged airspace violation may be linked to rescue or surveillance operations carried out by Finland following damage sustained by a cargo ship in the Gulf of Finland,\" public broadcaster YLE cited Defense Minister Antti Hakkanen as saying.\n\nThe ministry added the helicopter could have penetrated up to 4.1 kilometers (2.5 miles) into Finnish territory.\n\nWhat do we know about the cargo ship attack?\n\nEarlier Saturday, Finland — one of NATO's newest members — said a Russian cargo ship heading for Russia's Baltic exclave of Kaliningrad caught fire after being struck by drones in the Gulf of Finland.\n\nThe Finnish military said the Sparta II was damaged west of Russia's Gogland island, about 40 kilometers (25 miles) from Finland's coast, and later drifted into Finnish territorial waters.\n\nFinnish Border Guard Commander Ilja Iljin later told YLE that the vessel, which is known to have links to the Russian military, was struck by Ukrainian drones while in Russian waters.\n\n\"At the moment, there is no confirmed information about what cargo is on board, but it cannot be ruled out that there is military materiel on board,\" Iljin said.\n\nThe ship is on a US sanctions list, according to a search of the Open Sanctions website.\n\nThe Border Guard later said the crew of the Sparta II was evacuating into a life raft and rescue boat.\n\nOrpo backs Ukraine against 'aggressor'\n\n\"The [Ukraine] war is spilling over into our neighbouring areas,\" wrote Finnish Prime Minister Petteri Orpo on X.\n\nUkraine has the right to fight against the aggressor,\" he added.\n\nThe Finnish government has put temporary curbs on aviation and maritime traffic in the eastern Gulf of Finland.\n\nThe Defense Ministry said Finland had informed its allies about the incident.",
