    title: "US: Protesters demand human control over AI after Anthropic's IPO",
    summary: "Protesters gathered outside Anthropic’s San Francisco headquarters on 19 November 2026 to demand tighter regulation and greater human control over artificial intelligence, following the company’s $2 trillion stock market debut.",
    preview: "Armed with placards and banners, demonstrators outside Anthropic’s San Francisco offices urged authorities to rein in the breakneck pace of AI development. \"ASI is not a race, build it at a human pace,\" crowds chanted, while others called out, \"What's our goal? Human control.\" Signs reading \"Ban RSI\" and \"RSI - Really stupid idea\" took direct aim at recursive self-improvement, the mechanism allowing AI systems to upgrade their own intelligence without human intervention.",
    body: "Armed with placards and banners, demonstrators outside Anthropic’s San Francisco offices urged authorities to rein in the breakneck pace of AI development. \"ASI is not a race, build it at a human pace,\" crowds chanted, while others called out, \"What's our goal? Human control.\" Signs reading \"Ban RSI\" and \"RSI - Really stupid idea\" took direct aim at recursive self-improvement, the mechanism allowing AI systems to upgrade their own intelligence without human intervention. The rally took place against a backdrop of mounting debate over AI’s impact on society, and on the heels of Anthropic’s hugely anticipated IPO, which captivated investors despite market jitters and warnings of a tech bubble. Ahead, the company faces tougher scrutiny from a Democratic-led US Congress next year, while rival OpenAI has reportedly postponed its own flotation until 2027. For the protesters in San Francisco, the issue went far beyond financial metrics: their demands centred on strict government regulation, public accountability and guaranteeing that human beings never relinquish control over increasingly powerful machines.",
